-- To-do 268 (Midsummer Fire Festival: 656 spots have the same event creature twice):
-- Cause: the Cata/MoP Midsummer spawn set (game_event_creature guid 369498-370785, event 1) was imported on top of the older set (guid 352000-353999) without removing the old one; verified on dev 1-11: all 657 deleted guids have a surviving same-entry same-position twin in event 1.
-- Change: delete the 657 duplicate rows (game_event_creature, creature_addon, creature); 3 bonfires of the surviving set (352728, 352929, 352930) hang 10-18 yd in the air at pre-Cata terrain height: take the Z of the removed twin (369963, 369700, 369703).
-- Source: world DB itself (twin check on dev) + Cata Midsummer set; no retail sniff.
-- Rollback: rollback/268_midsummer_dupes_rollback.sql (re-inserts the 657 creature rows with the 3 old Z values; game_event_creature rows: INSERT (eventEntry 1, guid)).
-- Fix for Midsummer Fire Festival duplicate event creatures (Issue 268)
